      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "1. Project Status and Schedule"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "[PERSON_2] presented the current project status. The installation of the automated small parts warehouse with 18,000 container spaces has been completed mechanically. The two shuttle aisles and the conveyor loop to the picking stations have been installed, and the electrical commissioning started two weeks ago. The project is therefore about three weeks behind the baseline schedule approved by the steering committee in March."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The main cause of the delay is the late delivery of the control cabinets for the conveyor system, which [ORG_2] received from its subcontractor five weeks later than planned. [PERSON_6] explained that the integrator has deployed an additional commissioning team since the beginning of the month to recover part of the delay. Based on the revised plan, the trial operation can start in week 46, and the go-live of the new warehouse is now planned for the week after the plant shutdown in January instead of early December."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "[PERSON_4] reported that the interface between the warehouse management system and the ERP system has passed the first integration test. 214 of 236 test cases were completed successfully. The remaining 22 cases mainly concern returns and stock corrections and are expected to be resolved by the end of the month."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "2. Budget and Costs"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "[PERSON_5] presented the budget status. Of the approved total budget of "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ],
            "text": "EUR 4.8 million"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", EUR 3.9 million has been committed and EUR 3.1 million has already been invoiced. The forecast for the total project costs currently stands at EUR 4.95 million, which is EUR 150,000 above the approved budget."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The overrun results from additional costs for fire protection measures required by the building authority (EUR 95,000) and from extended support by the integrator during the longer commissioning phase (EUR 55,000). [PERSON_6] confirmed that [ORG_2] will bear the costs of the additional commissioning team itself, since the delay was caused by its subcontractor. The steering committee asked the project manager to check whether the remaining contingency of EUR 60,000 can partially cover the additional costs."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "3. Risks and Open Issues"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The following risks were discussed:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ],
                    "text": "Go-live in January:"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " the new date falls in the period with the highest order volume for spare parts after the turn of the year. [PERSON_3] considers this manageable if the old warehouse remains available as a fallback for four weeks."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ],
                    "text": "Staff training:"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " 26 warehouse employees still need to be trained on the new picking stations. Training cannot start until the trial operation begins."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ],
                    "text": "Data migration:"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " the master data of around 9,400 articles must be cleaned up before migration, in particular the packaging dimensions and weights. The logistics team has completed about 60 percent of this work."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ],
                    "text": "Spare parts for the shuttle system:"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " the service contract with [ORG_2] has not yet been signed. The draft is currently being reviewed by the purchasing department."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
